  tags: [implemented]
- label: counter adapter fetches a JSON endpoint (params.url) and extracts a numeric value via params.json_path (dot/bracket notation); supports env var interpolation in headers (interpolateEnvVars at fetch time), optional compare_url for trend calculation; resolveJsonPath uses Object.hasOwn to prevent prototype traversal at runtime, and config-validate.ts rejects dangerous path segments (__proto__, constructor, prototype) at config time
  command: test -f src/adapters/counter.ts && grep -q 'counter' src/adapters/adapter-registry.ts && grep -q 'resolveJsonPath' src/adapters/counter.ts && grep -q 'Object.hasOwn' src/adapters/counter.ts && grep -q 'DANGEROUS_PATH_SEGMENTS' src/config-validate.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: counter adapter items are deduped by URL in the DB layer via INSERT OR REPLACE and the dedupWinnerSubquery; since all fetches from the same counter endpoint share the same url field, only the latest value is kept per panel
