## contract
- label: refresh_interval belongs on IngestAdapterConfig (adapters[] ingest YAML), not on AdapterConfig passed to Adapter.fetch
  command: ! grep -A5 'export interface AdapterConfig {' src/adapters/types.ts | grep -q refresh_interval && grep -A10 'export interface IngestAdapterConfig' src/config/domain.ts | grep -q 'refresh_interval?:' && grep -q 'refresh_interval is ingest-only (IngestAdapterConfig), not on fetch contract' src/types.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- When a source fails to fetch (network error, bad response, parse error), the log and error message clearly identify which source had the problem
- mastodon, lobsters, youtube, podcast, stackexchange, and github adapters previously swallowed fetch errors (non-2xx, network, parse) via console.warn + return [] or null; after minimal fixes they now throw Error messages starting with '<name>: ' (e.g. 'mastodon: failed to fetch...') per the Adapter contract documented in src/adapters/types.ts and oz1 @spec @implemented
- 18 of 19 adapters' fetch methods comply with the contract in types.ts: throw on network/!2xx/parse/auth errors with name: prefix using errorMessage helper (twitter intentionally returns []+log without attempting fetch per its ox1 design; bookmarks has no network fetch; explicit no-sources [] only in configured cases for others) @spec @implemented
- The .facts file, relevant adapter source, and their .test.ts were updated (minimal diffs) so that contract-violating swallow behaviors are removed and tests assert the throwing behavior instead; no unrelated changes, no new features (e.g. no reddit OAuth) @spec @implemented

## reddit
- reddit adapter fetch for any public subreddit always fails with 403 (message starts with 'reddit: failed to fetch ...: 403' or wrapped); confirmed even using browser User-Agent + Accept headers on both www.reddit.com and old.reddit.com (upstream blocking of unauthenticated .json API access; not fixable with headers/UA; requires OAuth app + credentials or authenticated session) @spec @implemented
- config.example.yaml documents reddit as commented example (with note that it requires credentials due to upstream 403; no functional change to yaml; other presets untouched per smallest-change scope) @spec @implemented

## out-of-box
- Of the 19 adapters, the following work out-of-the-box returning real public content with no credentials/secrets (using only basic params from config.example or defaults): hackernews, lobsters, devto, arxiv, rss, wikipedia, stackexchange, npm (keywords), lemmy, producthunt, podcast (public feeds), youtube (public channels), github (trending mode and releases atom mode), mastodon (with hashtags or accounts), github-releases (anon in some envs; caveats per nzg), bookmarks (config-only, no network) @spec @implemented
- Live one-by-one re-tests (bun -e imports + fetch with configs from *.test.ts and config.*.yaml) confirm: reddit and twitter cannot work out-of-the-box without credentials; the other 15 (incl. github-releases with anon caveats per nzg) can (with caveats for mastodon some endpoints); reddit root cause is upstream 403 on public .json not solvable without auth @spec @implemented

## twitter
- twitter adapter never returns real Items out-of-the-box; it always logs a message about requiring credentials and returns [] (even if lists/searches configured); this is by design as it has no unauthenticated public fetch path @spec @implemented

## github-releases
- github-releases adapter (the dedicated API one) can return real release Items with anon unauth request in some environments (e.g. low rate), but may receive 403 or rate limit errors on api.github.com without token param; its error path correctly throws 'github-releases: ' per contract (unlike some other adapters) @spec @implemented

