# packaging

## docker
- label: GitHub Actions publishes the Docker image for both linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 platforms so Apple Silicon users can run ghcr.io/av/pace:latest
  command: grep -q 'platforms: linux/amd64,linux/arm64' .github/workflows/docker.yml
  tags: [spec, implemented]

# domain
- a Dashboard is the self-hosted web interface that displays aggregated, deduplicated, and optionally LLM-processed content from many sources in a single customizable view
- a Source is a content provider (Hacker News, Reddit, arXiv, RSS feeds, GitHub releases, podcasts, etc.) that a user configures to pull Items into the Dashboard
- an Item is a single piece of content (story, paper, video, release note, etc.) shown in the Dashboard, with title, link, publication time, and optional summary or body
- a Panel is a section of the Dashboard that shows a curated list of Items from one or more Sources after the user's configured Transforms have been applied
- a Transform is a processing step (deduplicate, keyword filter/exclude, keep latest N, LLM summarize/rank/filter, time decay scoring, etc.) that the user declares in their Config to control which Items appear and in what order
- a Config is the single YAML file in which the user declares adapters[] (optional refresh_interval per ingest entry on IngestAdapterConfig; Adapter.fetch contract is type+params only), optional pipelines, Transforms, the recursive flexbox Layout of Panels and Widgets (panel source objects only adapter and params), and optional LLM provider settings
- a Preset is a ready-to-use Config file (tech-news, ml-ai, academic-papers, product-launches, etc.) that can be selected with --preset or -P so a user can get a working Dashboard instantly without writing YAML
- a Refresh updates the Items for a Panel (or all Panels) by re-fetching from the underlying Sources, re-applying Transforms, and redrawing the Dashboard; users can trigger it manually via a button or it happens on the schedule defined per adapters[] entry (and per pipeline when configured), not on panel layout source objects
- LLM-powered Transforms (summarize, filter, rank by interests) are optional; when no LLM is configured or the provider is unreachable, the Dashboard still works normally using only the non-LLM Transforms
- the entire system runs as a single Docker container (or local Bun process) serving server-rendered HTML with no client-side JavaScript; the Dashboard is responsive and works on phones, tablets, and desktops
- a Widget is a layout node that displays static content (an image, text/markdown, or embedded iframe) rather than adapter-sourced Items; widgets are not Panels and are skipped by collectPanels @implemented
- a Share Storage Backend is a storage target such as GitHub Gist that saves Static Dashboard artifacts and returns an artifact identifier or raw artifact URL @implemented
- a Static Dashboard is a read-only snapshot of a Dashboard rendered to portable files that can be opened without running a pace server @implemented
- a Share Renderer is a service such as gisthost.github.io or gistpreview.github.io that turns stored Static Dashboard artifacts into a browser-rendered share URL @implemented

# content

## dedup
- Items from different Sources that point to the same story are automatically deduplicated so a user does not see the same link multiple times in one Panel

## filtering
- Users can add keyword filters or excludes in their Config so that, for example, hiring posts or off-topic content never appear in the Dashboard

# usage
- label: pace export writes the active config's rss/podcast feed URLs as OPML 2.0 (one folder per adapter) that round-trips through pace import; non-feed adapters and duplicate URLs are skipped with a warning
  command: bun test src/cli-export.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: GET /api/search?q=terms searches all stored deduped items (whole database, not just rendered panels) matching every whitespace-separated term case-insensitively in title, url, source, summary, or body, newest first with a panel field per hit; ?panel= scopes to one panel, ?limit= (1-500, default 50) caps results, and LIKE wildcards match literally
  command: bun test src/server/api-search.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: GET /api/search.rss?q=terms renders the same server-side search as an RSS 2.0 saved-search feed: channel titled after the query, newest hit as lastBuildDate, self link keeping the query string, and the same term semantics, ?panel= scoping, and ?limit= validation as the JSON endpoint
  command: bun test src/server/api-search-rss.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: A starred:yes or starred:no term in an /api/search or /api/search.rss query filters hits by star state via the same dedup identity stars are saved under (an operator-only query lists that whole star state), any other starred:* value is a 400 naming the valid forms, and the normalized operator is echoed in the JSON query field and the RSS channel title
  command: bun test src/server/api-search.test.ts src/server/api-search-rss.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'starred'
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: Pressing x on the dashboard toggles the focused item's seen state: seen items render dimmed, the state persists server-side in SQLite keyed by the item's dedup identity (normalized url, or id when url is empty) so it survives refreshes and is shared across browsers; GET /api/seen lists the seen keys and POST /api/seen {key, seen} sets one, with the same cross-site guard as refresh
  command: bun test src/server/api-seen.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: Opening an item's title link on the dashboard (Enter, click, or middle-click) automatically marks the item seen through the same persisted /api/seen state as the x key, dimming its duplicates on other panels too; re-opening an already-seen item never unmarks it, and static/no-JS pages are unaffected
  command: bun test src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'autoSeenItem|opening an item'
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: Pressing a on the dashboard marks every item in the focused panel seen at once (or unmarks them all when every item already is), persisted through POST /api/seen accepting a bulk {keys, seen} body of up to 500 validated keys applied atomically in one transaction, with the same cross-site guard as single marks
  command: bun test src/server/api-seen.test.ts src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: Pressing Shift+X on the dashboard toggles hide-seen mode: items marked seen are hidden from every panel (j/k navigation skips them and panels left with only seen items are dimmed), pressing it again shows them; the mode persists per browser in localStorage (pace.hide-seen) and is restored on load, and static/no-JS pages are unaffected
  command: bun test src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'hide-seen'
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: The dashboard injects mouse affordances for the keyboard actions: a collapse chevron (collapse-btn) and a mark-panel-seen check (panel-seen-btn) in each panel header next to refresh, and a per-item mark-seen button (item-seen-btn) shown on item hover/focus, each driving the same collapse/seen logic as the c/a/x keys with synced aria state; all are client-injected by dashboard.js so static/no-JS pages never render them
  command: bun test src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'mouse affordance'
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: Top-level notify: config rules POST new matching items (min_score and/or keywords, optional panel-id scope) as JSON to a webhook after each refresh; a SQLite notified_items ledger keyed by (rule criteria, item dedup identity) guarantees at-most-once delivery per rule, failed deliveries (non-2xx or 10s timeout) retry next refresh without failing the refresh, and ledger rows age out with retention once no stored item carries the key
  command: bun test src/notify.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: The interactive dashboard's / filter bar shows an RSS subscribe link whenever the query has terms, pointing at /api/search.rss?q= for the normalized terms (base_path respected); the link hides when the query is empty and the bar (including the link) is client-injected so servers and static exports never render it
  command: bun test src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: A notify rule's optional format field renders deliveries for a service preset - ntfy (plain text plus X-Title/X-Click headers), discord (webhook markdown content capped under 2000 chars by folding overflow into an and-N-more line), slack (incoming-webhook mrkdwn with links), or the default raw json payload - with per-service escaping, config-check validation of the preset name, pace notify test honoring it, and no effect on matching or the notified_items ledger
  command: bun test src/notify-format.test.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: The dashboard injects a fixed top-right toolbar (page-toolbar) with clickable equivalents of the page-wide keys - a theme toggle (theme-btn, label naming the theme a click switches to), a hide-seen toggle (hide-seen-btn, aria-pressed synced with the mode), and a help button (help-btn) - each driving the same logic as the t/Shift+X/? keys; the toolbar is client-injected by dashboard.js so static/no-JS pages never render it
  command: bun test src/dashboard-keyboard.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'toolbar'
